### Description

Etymology App failed to launch with error that Header's referrer is missing when run against .NET 7.0.

### Reproduction Steps


**Repro steps for the Problematic App:**
This is 5.0 app, issue occurs when we run against .NET 7.0

1.Launch Etymology.Web.exe from Etymology.
2.Open Edge https://localhost:5001.  

**Minimal Repro steps:**
1.Create a new web project.
2.Create a settings.json.
```
{
  "IndexPagePaths": [ "/", "/index.htm" ]
}
```
3.Create Settings.cs.
```c#
    public class Settings
    {
        public List<string> IndexPagePaths { get; } = new();
    }
```
4.Input the following code in startup.cs.
```c#
        public Startup()
        {
            IConfigurationBuilder configurationBuilder = new ConfigurationBuilder();
            configurationBuilder.AddJsonFile(Path.Combine("settings.json"), optional: false, reloadOnChange: true);
            this.configuration = configurationBuilder.Build();
        }

        public static IServiceCollection AddSettings<TSettings>(this IServiceCollection services, IConfiguration configuration, out TSettings settings)
            where TSettings : class
        {
            settings = configuration.Get<TSettings>();
            return services.AddSingleton(settings);
        }

        public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
        { 
            services.AddSettings(this.configuration, out Settings settings);
            if (settings.IndexPagePaths.Count == 0) 
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Can't get IndexPagePaths!");
            };
            services.AddRazorPages();
        }
```
5.When use default sdk 5.0, settings.IndexPagePaths.Count == 2.
When use sdk 7.0, settings.IndexPagePaths.Count == 0.

### Expected behavior

Web page should load successfully.

### Actual behavior

It shows an error: Header's referrer is missing.

### Regression?

Yes

Verify Scenarios:
1). Windows rs5 x64 + dotnet-sdk-7.0.100-alpha.1.21568.2: Fail
2). Windows rs5 x64 + dotnet-sdk-5.0.404-win-x64:Pass
3). Windows rs5 x64 + dotnet-sdk-6.0.101:Pass

### Known Workarounds

It will work after changing 

```c#
public List<string> IndexPagePaths { get; } = new(); 
```
to 

```c#
public List<string> IndexPagePaths { get; set;} = new();
```


### Configuration

**Application Name**: Etymology
**OS**: Windows 10 RS5
**CPU:** X64
**.NET Build Number:** dotnet-sdk-7.0.100-alpha.1.21568.2

**App Github Repo link:** https://github.com/Dixin/Etymology

**App, App Source and Minimal Repro Code checking at:**  https://devdiv.visualstudio.com/DevDiv/_workitems/edit/1458234

